llvm-4.0.0 backport patch: SinkThenElseCodeToEnd takes two unconditional arcs only (PS4)

This patch CHANGES CODE GENERATION for an end block reached by more than
two arcs or by a conditional arc beside the unconditional ones. r280364
(James Molloy, 2016-09-01, "[SimplifyCFG] Handle tail-sinking of more than
2 incoming branches", llvm-project 88cad7e5cf, first release LLVM 4.0)
lifted r279460's restriction (exactly two predecessors, both unconditional
branches) and splits the unconditional arcs off into a .sink.split block
when the end block has one conditional incoming arc (`if (a) x = 1; else
if (b) x = 2;`). In the game region 104 joins entered by a conditional
arc keep two stores of different immediates at the ends of the two arms,
which r280364 would sink into one store of a phi (round 154B: control
flow rebuilt from the bytes); the split form with an immediate in every
arm occurs once (0x69600a), where a ternary assigned and then stored
gives it without the rule. With this patch 0xf170d0 compiles to the
base's bytes and no matched game row changes. r279460 itself (the
sinking with a PHI of differing operands; the matched 0x1393600's
cmovge) stays.

--- a/lib/Transforms/Utils/SimplifyCFG.cpp	2026-11-11 07:49:07.285121853 +0000
+++ b/lib/Transforms/Utils/SimplifyCFG.cpp	2026-11-11 07:49:07.293956982 +0000
@@ -1735,7 +1735,11 @@
     else
       return false;
   }
-  if (UnconditionalPreds.size() < 2)
+  // PS4: the end block takes exactly two predecessors, both unconditional
+  // branches, as r279460 had it; r280364 (sinking from more than two arcs
+  // and from the unconditional arcs beside one conditional one, through a
+  // split block) is not taken.
+  if (Cond || UnconditionalPreds.size() != 2)
     return false;
   
   bool Changed = false;
